error[V0001]: this text is made right here, but this call needs text stored in a name, because its result is part of it; store it with `let` first, then use that
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0001_trim_on_call_result/main.vr:6:22
  |
6 |     println!("[{}]", read_line().trim());
  |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^ this text is made right here, but this call needs text stored in a name, because its result is part of it; store it with `let` first, then use that
  |
  = note: in Rust terms, the result is a reference into the value the call is made on, and Varyk only lets it point into a value stored in a `let`, not into a temporary one
